#edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97015a4a-5c53-5378-8e05-a56fb36ed8e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171389 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171389 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171389 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "976adf93-dc43-5e30-b5ea-cde860373a4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171390 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171390 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171390 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1e3422f-e66e-5a42-bf7e-aabddf3aa8d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171391 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171391 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171391 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ef6cac8b-6d55-5f26-a7de-4324c08ad778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171392 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171392 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171392 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e9e81b1-3ba2-53bf-a988-4476adbb310f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171837 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171837 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]?$\n\nI. $p: \\{ 0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n\nII. $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [ 0, 1 ]$\n\nIII. $r: [0,1] \\to [ 0, 1 )$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b0e57b0-a667-5bb2-bb1e-69c4d39b799e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171837 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f: X \\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $\\mathbb{R},$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[ 0, 1 ],$ the interval from $0$ and $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[ 0, 1),$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ but not including $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171838 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171838 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\nI. $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nII. $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n\nIII. $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171838 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "686f5d13-dfe9-5434-abff-052c7a4b76ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171838 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $\\mathbb Q,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171839 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171839 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3?$\n\nI. $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n\nII. $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n\nIII. $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171839 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c02bc2d0-fccb-5fbe-8914-c42ebc7bb9fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171839 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $g(x)=x-x^3$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x-x^3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x \\mapsto x-x^3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171840 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171840 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}?$\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171840 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "086ea590-785a-539d-8b0f-b69ac7301ce4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171840 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation \n\n$$\ng: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$ to the set $\\mathbb{R}.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\},$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1039 "Interpreting the Arrow Function Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172031 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172032 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172032 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172628 #edb/ref 175921860454