92186360316 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b6c6cc1d-2128-5296-a1bf-5ba24546bff3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186358727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360400 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e28754de-f3b9-5f94-af58-77ca7f67bf70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470527 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470528 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470529 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96745" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions has the domain ${1,2}?$\n- **I.** $p:{1,2}\\to R$\n- **II.** $q:R\\to [1,2)$\n- **III.** $r:[1,2)\\to {1,2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29b22caa-a284-5c7f-8948-ff4f4a184ce4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360705 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is ${1,2},$ the set containing the two numbers $1$ and $2$ only.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $[1,2),$ the interval from $1$ to $2$ (including $1$ but not including $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set of real numbers.\"*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31ddb8b3-b422-5344-82ab-b45add22b7cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360707 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set of real numbers\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $g:Q\\to R$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $Q,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $h(x)=x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c4078cd-00a3-5cec-bb89-1bbd7fc0f112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360712 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $h(x)=x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh:x↦x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96820" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $h:x↦{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be0479d2-daa4-53ca-93d6-5cafceecb447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360713 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $h:x↦{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to ${x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470536 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470537 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470538 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:R\\to R?$\n- **I.** The domain of $g$ is $R$\n- **II.** The codomain of $g$ is $R$\n- **III.** The range of $g$ is $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af009dba-f7f5-5f73-94d4-82504fdd6317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360716 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation \n\n$$\ng:R\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $R$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $R,$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470542 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470543 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186470544 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96830" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/74/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d79f788-f655-5287-8607-5b096289e0bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360719 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186461383 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461383 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461383 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6cd5dc92-6122-5f66-902b-cf7afd5b3037" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461384 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461384 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461384 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4df0471-5db6-5210-9df4-d5ba3514d0e2" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461385 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461385 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461385 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2e1150f-e231-56c5-81bd-1920108321f8" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186461386 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592